	number = {3},
	pages = {392 - 411},
	doi = {10.1134/S1064230726700280},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105048160325?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Abstract: The optimal control problem is considered. Its solution is sought in the class of functions that can be implemented on the onboard processor of the controlled plant. First, the problem of synthesizing a universal motion stabilization system is solved. To this end, a set of possible trajectories and a set of initial states are specified, and a single universal system is constructed that stabilizes the motion of the plant along all the given trajectories from all the given initial states. To obtain a mathematical expression for the function of the universal stabilization system, the method of symbolic regression is employed. A new symbolic regression technique, the universal code, is described; it combines all the advantages of well-known symbolic regression methods, genetic programming, Cartesian genetic programming, and the network operator method. After synthesizing the motion stabilization system, the optimal control problem is solved. A reference model is introduced into the plant control system, and the optimal control problem is solved for this model in the classical formulation. The reference model generates an optimal trajectory, while the universal stabilization system ensures high-quality motion of the plant in the vicinity of that trajectory. An example of solving the optimal control problem by the proposed method for a group of two quadcopters is presented. © Pleiades Publishing, Ltd. 2026.},
	type = {Article},
	publication_stage = {Final},
	source = {Scopus},
