	abstract = {Previous work has shown that mitigating potential vehicle control safety risks is becoming increasingly important with the development of autonomous driving systems. Although the security risks of camera-based sensors have been extensively and thoroughly researched, the vulnerability of relevant deep learning models for LiDAR-based sensors is still in the initial research stage. In this paper, we propose an attack method called Physical Point Attack (PPA) for generating perceptually 3D adversarial objects in a physical environment, which can be placed in front of the vehicle to fool LiDAR detectors. In contrast to existing work, our attack produces printable adversarial point clouds and maintains the perceptibility of the adversarial point clouds while remaining valid in real physical environments. Our code is available at https://github.com/chenxiaoyupetter/Physically-Realizable-Adversarial-Attacks-On-3D-Point-Cloud © 2022 IEEE.},
