	abstract = {Consistency checking of UML/OCL models is a challenging issue in software development. In this paper, we discuss an OWL/ontology-based method to detect the inconsistencies in the UML/OCL models as the first step of requirement change management. Specifically, we map the UML/OCL models to OWL, so that the consistency of the corresponding ontology can be checked by OWL reasoners automatically. We propose a set of mapping rules to interpret the components of UML state machine diagrams, along with OCL constraints, to OWL DL. Towards this objective, we demonstrate three consistency reasoning tasks over a state machine diagram using OWL reasoners. In each case, the result of reasoning is accompanied by an explanation of the logic behind the decision. © 2022 by SCITEPRESS–Science and Technology Publications, Lda. All rights reserved.},
