	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85079042034?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {In this paper, we propose an approach to checking consistency of temporal requirements for the behavior of concurrent systems. This approach is used in the early stages of formal verification of such systems to effectively identify contradicting and incompatible requirements. In this framework we use ontologies and ontological methods for dealing with temporal requirements. A set of requirements is represented as instances of classes of the Requirement Ontology. Instances of the Requirement Ontology classes have additional formal semantics defined by formulas of linear-Time temporal logic LTL. Based on this semantics, we define constraints on the values of class attributes for inconsistent requirements that cannot belong to the same set of requirements. We formally base the notion of requirement inconsistency. We implement the Requirement Ontology in the Protégé system and developed rules for detecting inconsistent patterns. © 2019 IEEE.},
